            "evidence": {
              "date": "Wed, Nov 18",
              "time": "2:30pm",
              "venue": "East Hall",
              "admission": "Free",
              "description": "Torus-equivariant cohomology classes of smooth projective varieties (e.g. flag varieties) are determined by their restrictions to fixed points. We'll compute these for Schubert classes in type A, using the 5-vertex model and colored extensions. The 6-vertex will be about the \"Chern-Schwartz-MacPherson\" deformations of Schubert classes. Then we'll introduce a trivalent analogue of R-matrices and use it to compute the products of Schubert classes, for up to 4-step flag varieties.",
              "end": "3:30pm"
            }
          },
